<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boryslav</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boryslav is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lviv">Lviv</a> Oblast in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>. From the mid-19th century it became the centre of the Galician oil industry, and in the early 20th century the oil basin around Boryslav and Drohobych made Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galicia">Galicia</a> one of the world's leading oil producers. Its oil workers were largely Jewish and Ukrainian.</p></div>
